# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AgenticQA Orchestrator Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 
# This file contains credentials and configuration for:
# - PostgreSQL + pgvector database
# - LLM (Language Model) for test generation  
# - Embedding models for self-healing
#
# ⚠️ SECURITY: Keep this file PRIVATE
#    Add to .gitignore and NEVER commit to version control
#
# See SETUP.md for detailed instructions on obtaining credentials
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE: PostgreSQL + pgvector  
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Required for: Test tracking, element storage, self-healing
# Default: postgresql://agenticqa:agenticqa@localhost:5432/agenticqa
# Start DB: docker compose up -d
#
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://agenticqa:agenticqa@localhost:5432/agenticqa

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM PROVIDER  —  pick ONE block below (both speak the OpenAI wire format)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Switching provider is CONFIGURATION, NOT CODE: set OPENAI_BASE_URL + OPENAI_API_KEY and the correct
# per-role model defaults follow automatically from `src/core/llm/modelCatalog.ts`, which detects the
# provider from the base URL. Leave every OPENAI_MODEL* var unset to use those defaults.
#
# Without any key the planner still works: 19 of 20 benchmark prompts are produced by the DETERMINISTIC
# path, which makes no LLM call at all. A key mainly buys knowledge-pack generation and Domain QA.
#
# ⚠️ Verify before trusting: `npm run probe:models` sends a one-token request per role.
#    404 = the ID is dead · 429 = alive, quota spent · 200 = good.
#    A dead ID does NOT look like a failure — the fallback chain hides it and the run just uses
#    something else. If results look odd, grep the log for "model … failed".
#
# [!] NEVER put a live key in this file. `.gitignore` excludes `.env`, NOT `.env.example` — this one is
#    committed on purpose, so anything written here becomes public. Put real keys in `.env`, or use the
#    extension's Settings panel, which stores them in your OS keychain.
#
# ▸ The VS Code extension's "AgenticQA: Settings" panel overrides these per-user without editing this
#   file (its key lives in VS Code SecretStorage); anything left blank there falls back to this file.

# ─── OPTION A — NVIDIA NIM  (recommended: free credit pool + 40 req/min, and it hosts Nemotron) ───
# Get a key: https://build.nvidia.com → sign in → "Get API Key". It looks like `nvapi-…`.
# Free tier is a CREDIT POOL (~1000) rather than OpenRouter's daily request cap, which suits the bursty
# benchmark runs this project does. Model IDs carry NO `:free` suffix — the whole hosted catalog draws
# on the same pool, so "free" is a property of the ACCOUNT, not the ID.
#
OPENAI_API_KEY=nvapi-YOUR_KEY_HERE
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
OPENAI_EMBED_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-embed-1b
#
# Per-role defaults applied automatically (override any of them below if you want):
#   planner / packgen  nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b   (MoE: 120B total, ~12B active — fast)
#   domainqa           nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
#   selfheal/reporter/explorer  openai/gpt-oss-20b
#   receptionist / casual       nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b
# Also available: nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b, minimaxai/minimax-m3, openai/gpt-oss-120b
#   (the last answers but took ~79s on a first call — avoid it for live roles).
# ❌ google/gemma-4-31b-it and z-ai/glm-5.2 never answered within 90s on a live key — don't use them.
#
# ✅ Embeddings: `nvidia/nv-embed-v1` is 4096-dimensional, which is exactly EMBEDDING_DIM — so switching
#    needs NO database reset. It is the generalist TEXT retriever; `nvidia/nv-embedcode-7b-v1` is the
#    same size but tuned for CODE retrieval, which this project never does (it embeds doc chunks, UI
#    element signatures and test knowledge). Prefer nv-embed-v1.

# ─── OPTION B — OpenRouter  (the historical default; free IDs end in `:free`) ────────────────
# Get a key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# ⚠️ Its free tier is a DAILY REQUEST CAP; a spent quota answers 429 and every role falls back.
#
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-YOUR_KEY_HERE
#OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#OPENAI_EMBED_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL OVERRIDES (optional)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Precedence (first that is set wins):
#   .agenticqa.json `models[role]`  >  OPENAI_MODEL_<ROLE>  >  OPENAI_MODEL  >  catalog default
#
# [!] OPENAI_MODEL is the "force ONE model for EVERY role" knob and it OVERRIDES the per-role defaults.
#    Leaving it set to a stale ID is exactly how the 2026-08-10 benchmark ran with all 8 roles issuing a
#    doomed request, taking a 404, and falling through the chain. **Prefer leaving it unset.**
#
#OPENAI_MODEL=
#
#OPENAI_MODEL_PLANNER=
#OPENAI_MODEL_PACKGEN=
#OPENAI_MODEL_DOMAINQA=
#OPENAI_MODEL_SELFHEAL=
#OPENAI_MODEL_REPORTER=
#OPENAI_MODEL_RECEPTIONIST=
#OPENAI_MODEL_CASUAL=
#OPENAI_MODEL_EXPLORER=

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Get free key: https://context7.com/dashboard
# Without this key, Context7 has lower rate limits and no private repo access
# The orchestrator will still work without this - it's optional enhancement
#
CONTEXT7_API_KEY=ctx7sk-YOUR_KEY_HERE

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI ANALYSIS (Optional, enables advanced AI-based analysis features)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
ENABLE_AI_ANALYSIS=true